From 68293f0c8b5f4d1b0022805241be7759547ad2fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:07:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): forward a worker node's archive of a relayed
 capability owner card home [daveey]

On a relay=home route the owner card exists only on the waiting card's home
gateway, so kanban_archive from the waiting card's run on a Board worker node
answered 'no such task' before the owner-card scope rule ran. When the local
lookup misses and the worker's task has a relay=home route naming that owner,
append a capability_owner_archive_requested event on the waiting card; the
home's dispatcher applies the same archive scope rule (archive_scope_for),
archives with the forwarded run on the archived event, and answers with a
capability_owner_archive_result the worker returns verbatim.
---
